---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE, url } from '../lib/site';
import { summary, brands } from '../lib/data';
import { fmtInt } from '../lib/format';
---
<Base title="About" description="Franchise Loan Stats is an independent, open-source project that turns the SBA's public loan file into a plain record of how loans to each franchise brand performed." crumbs={[{ name: 'About' }]}>
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>About Franchise Loan Stats</h1>
    <p class="lede">Buying a franchise often means signing a personal guarantee on a six- or seven-figure loan. The SBA publishes what happened to earlier borrowers. This site makes that record easy to read.</p>
    <h2>What it is</h2>
    <p>An independent reference built from the U.S. Small Business Administration's public 7(a) loan file: {fmtInt(summary.counts.loans_total)} loans, summarised for {fmtInt(brands.length)} franchise brands, plus industries, lenders and states. It is free to use and the brand table is free to download.</p>
    <h2>How it is made</h2>
    <p>A published data pipeline downloads the SBA files, matches loans to brands, computes the statistics and runs validation checks before anything goes live. Pages are generated by code from that output, so a figure on a page is always the figure in the data. Software agents, including AI coding assistants, help maintain the code and draft explanatory text under the owner's direction; they do not invent numbers. The <a href={SITE.repo}>source code is public</a> and the <a href={url('/methodology/')}>methodology</a> states every definition.</p>
    <h2>Who runs it</h2>
    <p>The site is built and operated by an independent data engineer. It has no connection to the SBA, any franchisor, any franchise broker or any lender, and no brand can pay to change its statistics.</p>
    <h2>How it is funded</h2>
    <p>Hosting is free and there are no paywalls. The site may carry clearly labelled sponsor placements or referral links in future; those never affect the data. See <a href={url('/disclosure/')}>how this site is funded</a>.</p>
    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>If a brand is matched wrongly or a figure looks off, write to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>. Franchisors are welcome to send context about a rebrand, sale or restructuring; factual corrections to brand matching are made in the public alias list.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
